                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 12 at 4:16AM MST until October 12 at 11:15AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Paria River in...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 1115 AM MST /1215 PM MDT/ Tonight.\n\n* At 416 AM MST /516 AM MDT/, a river gauge on the Paria River near\nUS-89 in southern Utah reported a rapid rise of 3 feet from\nthunderstorms that occurred on Sunday over the Paria River. Flash\nflooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Paria River.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nParia River.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLees Ferry and Vermilion Cliffs National Monument.\n\nThis includes the Colorado River near mile marker 0.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nLees Ferry Camp Site.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nParia River and Colorado River.",
                "instruction": "Get out of the Paria River slot canyon! Flood waters will flow down\nthe Paria River, reaching the confluence with the Colorado River at\nLees Ferry between 12 PM and 2 PM MST.\n\nGet out of washes and creeks if you are camping or hiking! Flooding\nis occurring or imminent and will inundate creeks and washes.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFWFGZ"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS55 KFGZ 121116"
                    ],
